           StripOnInput->False]},
         {
          ItemBox[
           PaneBox[
            
            StyleBox["\<\"EditAmaresMatrix[matrix] is used to edit the Amares \
fitting matrix which can be compressed or extended using\\nToFullAmaresMatrix \
or FromFullAmaresMatrix. \\nThe default properties are \\\"amp\\\": -1, \
\\\"sigma\\\": 0, \\\"gamma\\\": -1, \\\"shift\\\": -1, \\\"phase\\\": 0, \
\\\"B1\\\": False, \\\"init\\\": False.\\n\\nThe matrix has one row per \
metabolite and one column per fit property. For \\\"amp\\\", \\\"sigma\\\", \
\\\"gamma\\\", \\\"shift\\\" and \\\"phase\\\" the value sets how the \
parameter is shared between metabolites:\\n-1 (unique): the metabolite has \
its own free parameter.\\n0 (same): all metabolites with 0 share one common \
parameter.\\n1, 2, ... (group-01, group-02, ...): all metabolites with the \
same number share one parameter, different numbers are different \
parameters.\\n\\\"B1\\\" is True or False and switches the B1 (Ernst-angle) \
amplitude correction on or off for that metabolite.\\n\\\"init\\\" is True or \
False and selects the metabolites that are summed to the base spectrum used \
by AmaresInitialValues for the initial shift and linewidth \
calibration.\\n\\nEditAmaresMatrix[matrix, names] will do the same but will \
only do it for the values in the list names. If values are not in \
matrix\\nthey will be added, if values are names but not in matrix they will \
be removed from matrix.\"\>", "InformationUsageText",
             StripOnInput->False,
             LineSpacing->{1.5, 1.5, 3.}],
