contrast training data by blending the co-registered 3D datasets data1 and \
data2 in n linear steps\\nfrom data1 to data2. Each blend is normalized and \
the result is masked. The output is a 4D dataset where each blend is a \
channel.\\nMakeTrainData[{{data1, data2, n}, ..}] does the same for multiple \
pairs and joins all blends as channels, e.g. {{outph, inph, 6}, {wat, fat, \
5}}.\\nThe output can be used as data for PrepareTrainingData, during \
training a random channel is selected for each sample which acts as contrast \
augmentation.\"\>", "InformationUsageText",
