           StripOnInput->False]},
         {
          ItemBox[
           PaneBox[
            
            StyleBox["\<\"SplitDataForSegmentation[data] splits data for \
\\\"Legs\\\" segmentation, detecting left/right side and upper/lower leg \
position \\nautomatically using a classification \
network.\\nSplitDataForSegmentation[data, what] splits for the specified \
region. What can be any region accepted by SegmentData, i.e. \\\"Body\\\",\\n\
\\\"LegsBody\\\", \\\"LegsHipBody\\\", \\\"HipBody\\\", \
\\\"UpperLegsBody\\\", \\\"LowerLegsBody\\\", \\\"ShoulderBody\\\", \
\\\"Legs\\\", \\\"LegsHip\\\", \\\"UpperLegs\\\",\\n\\\"LowerLegs\\\", \
\\\"Hip\\\", \\\"Shoulder\\\", or \
\\\"Arm\\\".\\nSplitDataForSegmentation[data, seg] splits both data and \
segmentation identically for \\\"Legs\\\".\\nSplitDataForSegmentation[data, \
seg, what] does the same for the specified region.\\nOutput is {{patches, \
ranges, dim}, locations}.\"\>", "InformationUsageText",
             StripOnInput->False,
             LineSpacing->{1.5, 1.5, 3.}],
            FrameMargins->{{10, 10}, {8, 10}}],
