these separate kernels while NetTrain runs concurrently\\non its own kernel, \
which can substantially speed up training when augmentation is the \
bottleneck. If set to \\\"Parallel\\\",\\nthe older shared-queue \
Parallel-framework kernel pool is used instead. If set to {True, n} or \
{\\\"Parallel\\\", n} at most\\nn producer kernels are used, useful for \
debugging on a small scale. If set to False batches are generated in-process.\
